IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa17-helpers`

-- coa17-part21a-ch2-others.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 21A, Chapter 2 -- Information-gathering: the duties
-- on others, compliance, exemption and required particulars (ss 790G to 790L; lines 10351-10450 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. SOURCE, TARGET and HOW TO READ AN ANSWER are as in coa17-part21-ch1.l4 (JUST TRUE: the text
-- says yes; JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words; NOTHING: the text does not decide; a caller never turns NOTHING
-- into FALSE).
--
-- THE GATE. The duties of ss 790G to 790HA are a person's duties "in relation to a company", and by s 790B(1) this Part
-- applies to companies other than the excluded ones: each takes `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` as a seam
-- (MAYBE BOOLEAN; a JUST FALSE flows through; fork F4).
-- SEAMS. Schedule 1B (another part's) is behind s 790I; the notices of change are those of ss 790LD and 790LE.
-- TIME. "before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are
-- met": the last day is the day before the corresponding day of the next month, and the last day is in time (forks F2, F9).
-- NOT ENCODED HERE (machinery, inert reason 2 in NOTES.md): s 790IA (power to impose further duties involving nominee
-- shareholders), s 790K(5)-(6) and s 790L (powers to make or amend regulations).

-- FORKS in this module (NOTES.md, "Fork register (coa17)", gives each reading and the text that licenses it; the
-- coverage table points each row at its fork): F2 at s 790G(3), s 790H(3), s 790HA(3); F8 at s 790K(1), s 790K(2), s
-- 790K(3); F9 at s 790G(3), s 790H(3), s 790HA(3); F10 at s 790J(3).

§ `Part 21A Chapter 2: Information-gathering: duties on others, compliance, exemption, required particulars`

§§ `Duty to notify company on becoming PSC (s 790G)`

-- src:10353 | (1) This section applies to a person if—
-- src:10354 | (a) the person knows that they are a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company,
-- src:10355 | (b) the material in the register that is available for public inspection does not indicate the person’s status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10356 | (c) the person—
-- src:10357 | (i) has not informed the company of the person’s status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, or
-- src:10358 | (ii) has not given the company all of the required particulars of the person (see section 790K).
@ref s 790G(1) This section applies to a person if (src:10353-10358)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that they are a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material in the register that is available for public inspection indicates the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has informed the company of the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has given the company all of the required particulars of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790G(1) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF    `the person knows that they are a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
           AND (NOT `the material in the register that is available for public inspection indicates the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`)
           AND (   (NOT `the person has informed the company of the person's status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`)
                OR (NOT `the person has given the company all of the required particulars of the person`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person if— (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10360 | (a) inform the company of the person’s status as a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10361 | (b) give the company the required particulars (see section 790K).
@ref s 790G(2) The person must inform the company and give the company the required particulars (src:10360-10361)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790G(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790G(2) the person must inform the company of their status and give the company the required particulars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 790G(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person if" (the if fails)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 790G applies is not decided

-- src:10362 | (3) The person must comply with the duty in subsection (2) before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met.
@ref s 790G(3) before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met (src:10362)
GIVEN `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790G(3) the last day for the person to comply with the duty in subsection (2)` MEANS
    `s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met`

@ref s 790G(3) the person complied before the end of the period (src:10362)
GIVEN `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person complied` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790G(3) the person has complied with the duty in subsection (2) in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790G(3) the last day for the person to comply with the duty in subsection (2)` `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met`) `the day on which the person complied` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comply with the duty in subsection (2) before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met"

§§ `Duty to notify company of changes in PSC information (s 790H)`

-- src:10364 | (1) This section applies to a person if—
-- src:10365 | (a) the person knows that they are a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company,
-- src:10366 | (b) there has been a change in the required particulars of the person (see section 790K) and the person knows that to be the case, and
-- src:10367 | (c) the person has not informed the company of the change or has not given the company all of the information that the company would need to include in a notice of the change under section 790LD(1) or 790LE(1).
@ref s 790H(1) This section applies to a person if (src:10364-10367)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that they are a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has been a change in the required particulars of the person and the person knows that to be the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has informed the company of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has given the company all of the information that the company would need to include in a notice of the change under section 790LD(1) or 790LE(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790H(1) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF    `the person knows that they are a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
           AND `there has been a change in the required particulars of the person and the person knows that to be the case`
           AND (   (NOT `the person has informed the company of the change`)
                OR (NOT `the person has given the company all of the information that the company would need to include in a notice of the change under section 790LD(1) or 790LE(1)`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person if— (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10368 | (2) The person must—
-- src:10369 | (a) inform the company of the change, and
-- src:10370 | (b) give the company the information that the company would need to include in a notice of the change under section 790LD(1) or 790LE(1).
@ref s 790H(2) The person must inform the company of the change and give the company the information (src:10368-10370)
GIVEN `the answer under section 790H(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790H(2) the person must inform the company of the change and give the company the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer under section 790H(1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person if" (the if fails)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 790H applies is not decided

-- src:10371 | (3) The person must comply with the duty in subsection (2) before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met.
@ref s 790H(3) before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met (src:10371)
GIVEN `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 790H(3) the last day for the person to comply with the duty in subsection (2)` MEANS
    `s 790D(3) the last day of the period of one month beginning with the day` `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met`

@ref s 790H(3) the person complied before the end of the period (src:10371)
GIVEN `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person complied` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790H(3) the person has complied with the duty in subsection (2) in time` MEANS
    `s 790D(4)(b) the act was done by the last day of the period` (`s 790H(3) the last day for the person to comply with the duty in subsection (2)` `the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met`) `the day on which the person complied` `the day on which the question is asked` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comply with the duty in subsection (2) before the end of the period of one month beginning with the day on which the conditions in subsection (1) are met"

§§ `Duty to notify company of ceasing to be a PSC (s 790HA)`

-- src:10373 | (1) This section applies to a person if—
-- src:10374 | (a) the person knows that they have ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company,
-- src:10375 | (b) the material in the register that is available for public inspection does not indicate the person as having ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company, and
-- src:10376 | (c) the person has not informed the company of having ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company or has not informed the company of the date on which the person so ceased.
@ref s 790HA(1) This section applies to a person if (src:10373-10376)
GIVEN `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that they have ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material in the register that is available for public inspection indicates the person as having ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has informed the company of having ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has informed the company of the date on which the person so ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790HA(1) this section applies to the person` MEANS
    `s 790C(6) both answers hold`
        `s 790B(1) this Part applies to the company` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies to companies other than" (a JUST FALSE from s 790B(1) flows through)
        (IF    `the person knows that they have ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`
           AND (NOT `the material in the register that is available for public inspection indicates the person as having ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`)
           AND (   (NOT `the person has informed the company of having ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company`)
                OR (NOT `the person has informed the company of the date on which the person so ceased`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a person if— (a) ..., (b) ... and (c) ..." (the if fails)

-- src:10377 | (2) The person must inform the company—
-- src:10378 | (a) that the person has ceased to be a registrable person or a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company, and
-- src:10379 | (b) of the date on which the person so ceased.
@ref s 790HA(2) The person must inform the company that the person has ceased and of the date (src:10377-10379)
