§§ `Required particulars (s 790K)`

-- src:10414 | (1) The “required particulars” of an individual who is a registrable person are—
-- src:10415 | (a) name,
-- src:10416 | (b) a service address,
-- src:10417 | (c) the country or state (or part of the United Kingdom) in which the individual is usually resident,
-- src:10418 | (d) nationality,
-- src:10419 | (e) date of birth,
-- src:10420 | (f) usual residential address,
-- src:10421 | (g) the date on which the individual became a registrable person in relation to the company in question,
-- src:10422 | (h) the nature of his or her control over that company (see Schedule 1A), ...
-- src:10423 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 790K(1) The "required particulars" of an individual who is a registrable person (src:10414-10423)
DECLARE `s 790K particular` IS ONE OF
    `s 790K(1)(a) name`
    `s 790K(1)(b) a service address`
    `s 790K(1)(c) the country or state (or part of the United Kingdom) in which the individual is usually resident`
    `s 790K(1)(d) nationality`
    `s 790K(1)(e) date of birth`
    `s 790K(1)(f) usual residential address`
    `s 790K(1)(g) the date on which the individual became a registrable person in relation to the company in question`
    `s 790K(1)(h) the nature of his or her control over that company`
    `s 790K(2)(a) name`
    `s 790K(2)(b) principal office`
    `s 790K(2)(ba) a service address`
    `s 790K(2)(c) the legal form of the person and the law by which it is governed`
    `s 790K(2)(d) the date on which it became a registrable person in relation to the company in question`
    `s 790K(2)(e) the nature of its control over the company`
    `s 790K(3)(a) corporate or firm name`
    `s 790K(3)(b) principal office`
    `s 790K(3)(ba) a service address`
    `s 790K(3)(c) the legal form of the entity and the law by which it is governed`
    `s 790K(3)(d) if applicable, the register of companies in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`
    `s 790K(3)(e) the date on which it became a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company in question`
    `s 790K(3)(f) the nature of its control over that company`

`s 790K(1) the required particulars of an individual who is a registrable person` MEANS
    LIST
        `s 790K(1)(a) name`,
        `s 790K(1)(b) a service address`,
        `s 790K(1)(c) the country or state (or part of the United Kingdom) in which the individual is usually resident`,
        `s 790K(1)(d) nationality`,
        `s 790K(1)(e) date of birth`,
        `s 790K(1)(f) usual residential address`,
        `s 790K(1)(g) the date on which the individual became a registrable person in relation to the company in question`,
        `s 790K(1)(h) the nature of his or her control over that company`

-- src:10424 | (2) In the case of a person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12) as if the person were an individual, the “required particulars” are—
-- src:10425 | (a) name,
-- src:10426 | (b) principal office,
-- src:10427 | (ba) a service address,
-- src:10428 | (c) the legal form of the person and the law by which it is governed,
-- src:10429 | (d) the date on which it became a registrable person in relation to the company in question, and
-- src:10430 | (e) the nature of its control over the company (see Schedule 1A).
@ref s 790K(2) In the case of a person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12), the "required particulars" (src:10424-10430)
`s 790K(2) the required particulars of a person in relation to which this Part has effect as if the person were an individual` MEANS
    LIST
        `s 790K(2)(a) name`,
        `s 790K(2)(b) principal office`,
        `s 790K(2)(ba) a service address`,
        `s 790K(2)(c) the legal form of the person and the law by which it is governed`,
        `s 790K(2)(d) the date on which it became a registrable person in relation to the company in question`,
        `s 790K(2)(e) the nature of its control over the company`

-- src:10431 | (3) The “required particulars” of a registrable relevant legal entity are—
-- src:10432 | (a) corporate or firm name,
-- src:10433 | (b) ... principal office,
-- src:10434 | (ba) a service address,
-- src:10435 | (c) the legal form of the entity and the law by which it is governed,
-- src:10436 | (d) if applicable, the register of companies in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register,
-- src:10437 | (e) the date on which it became a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company in question, and
-- src:10438 | (f) the nature of its control over that company (see Schedule 1A).
@ref s 790K(3) The "required particulars" of a registrable relevant legal entity (src:10431-10438)
`s 790K(3) the required particulars of a registrable relevant legal entity` MEANS
    LIST
        `s 790K(3)(a) corporate or firm name`,
        `s 790K(3)(b) principal office`,
        `s 790K(3)(ba) a service address`,
        `s 790K(3)(c) the legal form of the entity and the law by which it is governed`,
        `s 790K(3)(d) if applicable, the register of companies in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register`,
        `s 790K(3)(e) the date on which it became a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company in question`,
        `s 790K(3)(f) the nature of its control over that company`

-- src:10414 | (1) The “required particulars” of an individual who is a registrable person are—
-- src:10415 | (a) name,
-- src:10416 | (b) a service address,
-- src:10417 | (c) the country or state (or part of the United Kingdom) in which the individual is usually resident,
-- src:10418 | (d) nationality,
-- src:10419 | (e) date of birth,
-- src:10420 | (f) usual residential address,
-- src:10421 | (g) the date on which the individual became a registrable person in relation to the company in question,
-- src:10422 | (h) the nature of his or her control over that company (see Schedule 1A), ...
-- src:10423 | (i) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 790K(1) the particular is a required particular of an individual who is a registrable person (src:10414-10423)
GIVEN particular IS A `s 790K particular`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790K(1) the particular is a required particular of an individual who is a registrable person` MEANS
    IF elem particular (`s 790K(1) the required particulars of an individual who is a registrable person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “required particulars” of an individual who is a registrable person are—" (a list closed by "are", not "only": fork F8)

-- src:10424 | (2) In the case of a person in relation to which this Part has effect by virtue of section 790C(12) as if the person were an individual, the “required particulars” are—
-- src:10425 | (a) name,
-- src:10426 | (b) principal office,
-- src:10427 | (ba) a service address,
-- src:10428 | (c) the legal form of the person and the law by which it is governed,
-- src:10429 | (d) the date on which it became a registrable person in relation to the company in question, and
-- src:10430 | (e) the nature of its control over the company (see Schedule 1A).
@ref s 790K(2) the particular is a required particular of a person treated as an individual (src:10424-10430)
GIVEN particular IS A `s 790K particular`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790K(2) the particular is a required particular of a person in relation to which this Part has effect as if the person were an individual` MEANS
    IF elem particular (`s 790K(2) the required particulars of a person in relation to which this Part has effect as if the person were an individual`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the “required particulars” are—" (a list closed by "are", not "only": fork F8)

-- src:10431 | (3) The “required particulars” of a registrable relevant legal entity are—
-- src:10432 | (a) corporate or firm name,
-- src:10433 | (b) ... principal office,
-- src:10434 | (ba) a service address,
-- src:10435 | (c) the legal form of the entity and the law by which it is governed,
-- src:10436 | (d) if applicable, the register of companies in which it is entered (including details of the state) and its registration number in that register,
-- src:10437 | (e) the date on which it became a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to the company in question, and
-- src:10438 | (f) the nature of its control over that company (see Schedule 1A).
@ref s 790K(3) the particular is a required particular of a registrable relevant legal entity (src:10431-10438)
GIVEN particular IS A `s 790K particular`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790K(3) the particular is a required particular of a registrable relevant legal entity` MEANS
    IF elem particular (`s 790K(3) the required particulars of a registrable relevant legal entity`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “required particulars” of a registrable relevant legal entity are—" (a list closed by "are", not "only": fork F8)

-- src:10439 | (4) In this section “name”, in relation to an individual, means the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 790K(4) "name", in relation to an individual, means the individual's forename and surname (src:10439)
GIVEN forename IS A STRING
      surname IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 790K(4) the name of the individual` MEANS CONCAT forename, " ", surname

-- src:10440 | (4A) Where an individual is a peer or an individual usually known by a title, any requirement imposed by this Act to provide the individual’s name because it forms part of the required particulars under this section may be satisfied by providing that title instead of the individual’s forename and surname.
@ref s 790K(4A) Where an individual is a peer or an individual usually known by a title (src:10440)
GIVEN `the individual is a peer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is usually known by a title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 790K(4A) the requirement to provide the individual's name may be satisfied by providing the title instead of the forename and surname` MEANS
    IF `the individual is a peer` OR `the individual is usually known by a title`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an individual is a peer or an individual usually known by a title"
